<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
CODM reviews income earned on marketable securities held in Trust Account to measure and monitor shareholder value and determine the
most effective strategy of investment with the Trust Account funds while maintaining compliance with the Trust Agreement.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Operating
expenses are reviewed and monitored by the CODM to manage and forecast cash to ensure enough capital is available to complete a business
combination or similar transaction within the business combination period. The CODM also reviews operating expenses to manage, maintain
and enforce all contractual agreements to ensure costs are aligned with all agreements and budget. Operating expenses, as reported on
the statements of operations and comprehensive income and loss, are the significant segment expenses provided to the CODM on a regular
basis.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0in; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

